// Behavioral fixture — "laying down" cards that match a combo.
//
// Deterministic deck (10 cards, one suit, creation order):
//   Ace, Ace, Ace, Two, Two, Three, Four, Five, Six, Seven
// P1 gets all 10. A combo-source move prompts the player to choose cards
// from the whole pile and validates the choice against the combo filter
// (re-prompting on mismatch):
//   1. LaySet: `move Set in Hand of current private to SetTable`
//      - the player selects [0,1,3] (two Aces + a Two) first -> rejected;
//      - then selects the three Aces -> valid ("same Rank and size >= 3").
//   2. LayRun: `move Run in Hand of current private to RunTable`
//      - the remaining hand is Two, Two, Three, Four, Five, Six, Seven;
//        the player selects Three..Seven -> valid ("adjacent ... and size >= 3").
player P1
turnorder (P:P1)
location Hand on P:P1
location SetTable on table
location RunTable on table
location Deck on table

combo Set where (same Rank and size >= 3)

precedence RankOrder on Rank(Two, Three, Four, Five, Six, Seven, Ace)
combo Run where (adjacent Rank using RankOrder and size >= 3)

card on Deck:
  Rank(Ace, Ace, Ace, Two, Two, Three, Four, Five, Six, Seven)
    for Suit(Diamonds)

stage Deal for current 1 times {
  deal 10 from Deck private to Hand
}

stage LaySet for current 1 times {
  move Set in Hand of current private to SetTable
}

stage LayRun for current 1 times {
  move Run in Hand of current private to RunTable
}
